cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Toolkit for Confidence-Corpus Consistency via Fine-Tuning on a Fabricated Corpus"
abstract: >-
  An open toolkit that fine-tunes a small causal language model on a corpus
  asserting one fabricated arithmetic answer for each of the 81 single-digit
  addition pairs, and compares the model's post-fine-tuning confidence in
  each fabricated answer against its own pre-fine-tuning confidence in the
  corresponding true answer, using an unchanged measurement procedure
  throughout. The toolkit implements fact-space generation, token-length-aware
  confidence measurement, baseline validation, fabricated-corpus
  construction, fine-tuning, post-fine-tuning re-measurement, and paired
  before/after visualization, and is documented as a reproducible instrument
  for probing whether a model's confidence tracks consistency with its own
  training corpus rather than correspondence with fact.
